# Business Connect: new form keys (frontend contract only)

The redesign adds four forms. They use the **same** frontend service and endpoint pattern as the existing forms:
`POST {VITE_API_URL}/api/forms/{formKey}`. No backend code was changed. Until the backend supports these keys,
the forms run in demo mode (browser-only) when `VITE_API_URL` is empty, and will fail with the normal error
message if `VITE_API_URL` points at a backend that does not know them yet.

Every submission also carries `lang`, `consent` and `page`, as for the existing forms.

| formKey | Used on | Fields (required marked *) |
|---|---|---|
| `quote` | Product page, Supplier page | subject*, name*, phone*, organisation, quantity, state, message |
| `supplier` | Business Connect (tab "List as a supplier") | organisation*, name*, phone*, email, supplierType*, state*, district, categories*, capacity, message |
| `sourcing` | Product Sourcing page | need*, quantity*, frequency, destination, spec, name*, organisation, phone*, email, message |
| `connect` | Business Connect | role*, name*, phone*, state*, offer*, organisation, email |

Option values: `supplierType` = farmer, fpo, manufacturer, supplier. `frequency` = once, monthly, seasonal, contract.
`role` = farmer, fpo, manufacturer, supplier, buyer.

Server-side validation, rate limiting and spam protection should follow the same rules as the existing forms.

## Marketplace and directory data
Products and suppliers live in `src/data/marketplace.js` and are **sample listings** (`sample: true`, `verified: false`).
They show only while `VITE_DRAFT_MODE` is not `false`. At launch replace them with real entries and set
`verified: true`; unverified entries are hidden automatically and the pages show an "opening soon" state.
The marketplace is enquiry based: no prices, cart or payment. Confirm the Federation's selling model
(marketplace/middleware or direct seller) with the client before changing this.

## Registration forms (fpo, vendor, projecthead, member, job)
See `docs/ADMIN_API.md`. The earlier `career` key was replaced by `job`.